According to items (a)--(c) of Lemma \ref{logalpha} applied to $\phi$ and $\phi^{-1}$ respectively, $H_{top}(\phi,U)=\log\alpha$ and $H_{top}(\phi^{-1},U)=\log \alpha^*$, where $\alpha$ is the value at which stabilizes the sequence $\alpha_n=\frac{c_{n+1}}{c_{n}}$ and $\alpha^*$ is the value at which stabilizes the sequence $\alpha^*_n=\frac{c_{n+1}^*}{c_{n}^*}$. For every $n>0$, since $\phi^n(C_n(\phi,U))=C_n(\phi^{-1},U)$, using that $\phi^n$ is an automorphism, and by Lemma \ref{Delta}(b), we have that
